<Defs>

	<ThingDef ParentName="CGF1_MWP_MachinePistol_T1">
		<defName>CGF1_MWP_Type80_Pistol_</defName>
		<label>Type 80 Pistol</label>
		<description>Caliber: 7.62x25mm Tokarev. 10-round detachable mag. Select-Fire.
		
The Type 80 is a Chinese machine pistol developed in the 1980s. Its external similiarities to the Mauser M712 Schnellfeuer are no coincidence as the C96 design was broadly the inspiration for the Type 80, with the mechanical operation being a general refinement of the Mauser design. The pistol was intended to be used by vehicle crews and special operations units that would be in need of a potent close-quarters weapon; consequently, the weapon also had features such as an optional pistol stock that contained a removable knife, and the ability to use extended magazines. However, problems with rapid overheating coupled with a mediocre effective range made the Type 80 unsuccessful in PLA service.</description>
